<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Pisa</h1><p class="st-meta">1085 CE – 1406 CE (approx.) · capital Pisa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Tuscan maritime republic that dominated the western Mediterranean in the 12th century and left the Piazza dei Miracoli with its famous leaning tower.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pisan fleets attacked Muslim bases in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in the 11th century, and booty from a raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> in 1063 paid for the cathedral. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consuls</a> governing the city are attested by 1085. Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-of-pisa">Daibert</a> led a Pisan fleet in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> built trading quarters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, ruled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a>, and conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> briefly in 1113–1115. Loyal to the emperors, it was a Ghibelline stronghold. Its merchants brought back Arabic learning: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fibonacci">Leonardo Fibonacci's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liber-abaci">Liber Abaci</a> of 1202 introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-arabic-numeral-system">Hindu-Arabic numerals</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The cathedral square, with baptistery and bell tower begun in 1173, shows its wealth.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a> destroyed the Pisan fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-meloria-1284">Meloria</a> in 1284, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> in 1324. Weakened by faction and the silting of its port, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> was sold to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-florence">Republic of Florence</a> in 1405 and surrendered after a siege in 1406.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-pisa.jpg" alt="Republic of Pisa" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_Pisa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1085 CE – 1406 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pisa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Daibert of Pisa, Ugolino della Gherardesca, Pietro Gambacorta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tuscan Italian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pisa, Commune of Pisa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1246&amp;focus=republic-of-pisa" aria-label="Republic of Pisa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4930 628 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Pisa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5250 884L5226 1028M5250 884L5233 973M5250 884L5252 8